+## Summary of changes
+
+**`src/_pytest/assertion/util.py`** — reworked `_compare_eq_sequence`:
+- It now computes `comparing_bytes = isinstance(left, bytes) and isinstance(right, bytes)`.
+- When comparing bytes, the "At index N diff: ..." line shows single-byte slices (`b'4' != b'1'`) instead of integer ordinals (`52 != 49`).
+- When comparing bytes, the "…first extra item: …" line shows the first extra byte as a slice (`b'4'`) instead of an int (`52`).
+- All non-`bytes` sequences keep exactly the previous behavior, so existing tests (`test_sequence_different_items`, `test_iterable_full_diff`, etc.) are unaffected.
