+
+- Added a small `PythonConfig` helper that only implements `getoption`, so `util.assertrepr_compare` can be exercised directly without relying on the deprecated global `pytest.config`.
+- Added the missing `callequal(left, right, verbose=False)` helper, which is what the linter was complaining about (`F821 undefined name 'callequal'`). It returns the list produced by `util.assertrepr_compare`, matching the list-based expectations in the tests.
+- Moved the two new tests into a `TestAssert_reprcompare` class so their `self` parameter is a real bound-method receiver (instead of being interpreted by pytest as a request for a `self` fixture).
+
+That resolves the reported `F821` errors. Note that the linter check only flags the undefined name; the actual runtime behavior of `test_bytes_index_diff_shown_as_bytes` also depends on `difflib.ndiff` behavior for `b"4"`/`b"1"` (it may emit `?` intraline guide lines), but that is a property of the existing assertion expectations rather than a syntax/name error, so I left the assertions untouched.
